Id: acc025w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_accounts
Controls: CIS 3.3, 5.1; NIST AC-2, AC-3; ISO 5.16, 5.18, 8.3; CE User access control

The user's home directory is on a filesystem that did not answer
within Tiger_Mount_Timeout seconds, which is what a hard NFS or CIFS
mount looks like when its server is down. The account's home-directory
checks (permissions, dotfiles, dormancy) were skipped rather than hang.
Other accounts with homes under the same parent directory are skipped
without being asked again. Bring the server back, or unmount the share,
and run again.
